{{RightToc}}Experience Tools provide a way to request persistent permissions across multiple logins and with multiple objects and scripts.  In order to use these functions, you must have an ''experience key''.  For further information, see [http://community.secondlife.com/t5/English-Knowledge-Base/Experiences-in-Second-Life/ta-p/2744686 Experiences in Second Life] in the Second Life Knowledge Base.

The Experience Tools API fall into three categories:

== Experience Information ==
{|
{{LSL DefineRow|integer|[[llAgentInExperience]](key agent)}}
{{LSL DefineRow|list|[[llGetExperienceDetails]](key experience_id)}}
|}

== Experience Permissions ==
{|
{{LSL DefineRow|event|[[experience_permissions]](key agent)}}
{{LSL DefineRow|event|[[experience_permissions_denied]](key agent, integer reason)}}
{{LSL DefineRow|void|[[llRequestExperiencePermissions]](key agent, string name)}}
|}

== Experience Persistent Storage==
The persistent storage of experiences can still be used even where the experience is not set up as an allowed experience.

Current limits for Persistent storage:
* Each key may be a maximum of 1011 bytes
* Each value may be a maximum of 4095 bytes
* Total stored data is restricted to 128 MiB

These are all asynchronous functions, they all return a {{LSLGC|Key/handle|handle}} that corresponds to a [[dataserver]] event.

{|
{{LSL DefineRow|key|[[llReadKeyValue]](string k)}}
{{LSL DefineRow|key|[[llCreateKeyValue]](string k, string v)}}
{{LSL DefineRow|key|[[llUpdateKeyValue]](string k, string v, integer checked, string original_value)}}
{{LSL DefineRow|key|[[llDeleteKeyValue]](string k)}}
|}

===Debugging===
{|
{{LSL DefineRow|key|[[llDataSizeKeyValue]]()|Gets the number of bytes used by the experience along with the experience's byte quote}}
{{LSL DefineRow|key|[[llKeysKeyValue]](integer start, integer count)|Gets the names of the keys}}
{{LSL DefineRow|key|[[llKeyCountKeyValue]]()|Gets the number of keys}}
{{LSL DefineRow|string|[[llGetExperienceErrorMessage]](integer value)|Converts an integer error code to a wordy string representation}}
|}
