* [[PRIM_LINK_TARGET]] is a special parameter which can be inserted to perform actions on multiple prims on the linkset with one call.
** Passing 0 (zero) as the link number in the formal link parameter on a linked object will return an empty list.
* The legacy value of [[PRIM_TYPE]], 1 (which is often referred to as PRIM_TYPE_LEGACY), is not supported by this function as a flag{{Footnote|[[llGetPrimitiveParams]] came after PRIM_TYPE_LEGACY was deprecated.|llGetPrimitiveParams came after PRIM_TYPE_LEGACY was deprecated.}}.
