|func_footnote
|func_desc=
The '''llLinksetDataFindKeys''' function returns a list of up to {{LSLP|count}} keys from the datastore that match {{LSLP|pattern}}, starting at the one indicated by {{LSLP|start}}. If {{LSLP|count}} is less than 1, then all keys between {{LSLP|start}} and the end which match {{LSLP|pattern}} are returned. If {{LSLP|count}} minus {{LSLP|start}} exceeds the number of matching keys, the returned list will be shorter than {{LSLP|count}}, down to a zero-length list if {{LSLP|start}} equals or exceeds the number of matching keys. The list is ordered alphabetically.
|func_footnote
|spec=
{{LSLP|pattern}} is a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regular_expression Regular expression].

|caveats=
*The maximum length for {{LSLP|pattern}} seems to be 800 characters.
*There seems to be a timing restriction. If the time limit is exceeded, the function fails silently.
**Returns an empty list and the script continues execution.
*To delete keys matching an expression, use the similar [[llLinksetDataDeleteFound]].
|helpers
|also_functions=
